WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.037
Step four reads the
Azure retirement in full.

2
00:00:03.037 --> 00:00:07.275
Its notice I D is azure,
R T five J six K L.

3
00:00:07.275 --> 00:00:10.216
It's due on September thirtieth, 2027,

4
00:00:10.216 --> 00:00:13.550
by the kit's rule, at
the advisory's end time.

5
00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:19.500
It names one public I P address,
and its fingerprint is a SHA-256.

6
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:22.365
Step five reads the same
fixtures a day later,

7
00:00:22.365 --> 00:00:26.625
as of November tenth, and compares
the fingerprints of the two runs.

8
00:00:26.625 --> 00:00:28.762
The same twenty-two notices come back,

9
00:00:28.762 --> 00:00:31.588
and the count of fingerprints
that differ is zero.

10
00:00:31.588 --> 00:00:35.637
A second read changes first seen
in the run, but no fingerprint,

11
00:00:35.637 --> 00:00:39.925
so the router in Module 7 sees
nothing new and makes no second task.

12
00:00:39.925 --> 00:00:43.845
Step six runs the record's
tests, for the notice record,

13
00:00:43.845 --> 00:00:48.300
the fingerprint, and times and
text: seventeen pass, none fail.

14
00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:50.210
Then delete the output folder.
